>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.orglett.6b00949","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/1543823.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Cp*⁻, Cl⁻ and an ortho-cyclometalated N–N ligand give a Rh(III) limiting form. Given the input atom inventory. The terminal N has no hydrogen. Partial multiple-bond character at N–N and the ortho C–Rh contact support a charge-separated N=N terminus and an aryl carbanion. Localized 11 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths.

